2026-04-29 15:58:39,831 | INFO | ai_app | {'request_id': 'd79bc1dd-093f-4633-98fb-451c90d5bf6e', 'stage': 'azure_ocr_text_extracted', 'invoice_id': 7005, 'raw_ocr_text': 'Consolidatedanalytics\n19712 MacArthur Blvd., Ste 110, Irvine, CA 92612\nTel. (949) 988-7200, (800) 320-9490\nwww.ConsolidatedAnalytics.com\nMay 3, 2019\nAnthony Meola\nWest Coast Advisory LLC\n12 Cavaillion\nNewport Coast, CA 92657\nDear Tony:\nOn behalf of CA Holding Company II, LLC (the "Company"), I am pleased to offer you the\nopportunity to serve on the Company\'s Board of Managers (the "Board") as an Independent\nManager. The term of your position as the Independent Manager will be effective April 29, 2019\npursuant to the Company\'s Amended and Restated Limited Liability Company Agreement, dated\nFebruary 1, 2019, by and among the Company and the Members identified therein (the\n"Operating Agreement"). This letter will serve to memorialize the terms of your membership on\nthe Board.\nAs an Independent Manager, you will perform such duties as prescribed in the Operating\nAgreement and will provide certain business services to the Company and its subsidiaries\n(collectively, the "Company Group") under the direction of the Board.\nAs compensation for your services, you will receive a $100,000 annual retainer, which shall be\npaid to West Coast Advisory LLC ("WCA") in monthly installments in arrears (provided, that if\nthe last day of a month is not a business day, such monthly installment will be made to you on\nthe following business day), and WCA will be reimbursed for all reasonable and documented\nout-of-pocket expenses directly related to your service as the Independent Manager of the\nCompany\'s Board in accordance with the Company Group\'s policies.\nAs additional compensation for your services, you will be granted an equity incentive equal 102\nClass P Units of the Company (the "Incentive Units"), representing approximately 0.5% of the\ncommon equity of the Company at the time of issuance. The Incentive Units will have a\nparticipation threshold of $1,000 per unit and will vest over five years subject to the terms and\nconditions provided in a Class P Unit Award Agreement (the "Award"), a copy of which will be\nprovided to you under separate cover; provided, however, that 100% of your unvested Incentive\nUnits shall vest immediately upon a Sale of the Company (as defined in the Operating\nAgreement) subject to your continued service to the Board through such date, unless otherwise\nset forth in the Award. The grant of the Incentive Units will be conditioned upon execution of a\nPage 1\nAmericasActive:13507544.3\nConfidentiality, Non-Solicitation and Non-Disparagement Agreement attached hereto as Exhibit\nA.\nPlease indicate your willingness to serve as an Independent Manager of the Company\'s Board,\non the terms set forth herein by your signature below. This offer is subject to Board and Member\napproval.\nSincerely,\nArvin Wijay\nChief Executive Officer\nAcknowledged and agreed, as of the date first above written:\nWEST COAST ADVISORY, LLC\nAnthony Meola, Manager\nPage 2\n5. The fair market value on the Grant Date of the property with respect to which the election is\nbeing made (determined without regard to any lapse restrictions, other than a non-lapse\nrestriction as defined in Treasury Regulation Section 1.83-3(h)), is: $0.\n6. The amount paid for such property: $0.\n7. The amount to include in gross income for the undersigned taxpayer with respect to the Company\nClass P Units is: $0.\nThe undersigned taxpayer will file this election with the Internal Revenue Service office with which\nthe taxpayer files his annual income tax return not later than 30 calendar days after the date of transfer of\nthe property. A copy of the election will also be furnished to the person for whom the services were\nperformed. The undersigned taxpayer is the person performing the services in connection with which the\nproperty was transferred.\nWEST COAST ADVISORY, LLC\n5Th\nDated:\n6.9.19\nBy:\nAnthony Meola, Manager\nAnnex B - 2\nSherri Puzzuto\nFrom:\nARVIN WIJAY\nSent:\nMonday, August 3, 2020 3:15 PM\nTo:\nSherri Puzzuto\nCc:\nMike Jones; Dana Gross; Lewis Ngo; AccountsPayable\nSubject:\nWest Coast Adviso...'}
